title: RDF-Rules is a rules system on RDF data
---
pub_date: 2026-11-22
---
author: Majid alDosari
---
body:

I recently released ['rdf-rules'](https://github.com/pnnl/rdf-rules/).

This was a culmination of systemizing ['BIM2RDF'](https://github.com/pnnl/bim2rdf/)
where the goal was to convert (very!) detailed building design data to RDF for interoperability.

It's so general that I think it can be thought of as some [formal system](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formal_system).
The logical limit of using 'rdf-rules' is that you can use a programming language (Python) to process data
and RDF to structure it.

I found this to be very satisfying as I can cast so much of data science work this way.
After an initial data ingest, everything can become a query
including structuring new derived data.
I also found that it enables team productivity because the only common skill needed
is to be able to author SPARQL queries (which could easily be AI generated these days).
You just need one programmer to set up the system initially.

